{"q":"169","t":"Majority Element","d":"Easy","p":false,"c":"<p>Given an array <code>nums</code> of size <code>n</code>, return <em>the majority element</em>.</p>\n\n<p>The majority element is the element that appears more than <code>&lfloor;n / 2&rfloor;</code> times. You may assume that the majority element always exists in the array.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums = [3,2,3]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 3\n</pre><p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums = [2,2,1,1,1,2,2]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 2\n</pre>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>n == nums.length</code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 5 * 10<sup>4</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>-10<sup>9</sup> &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 10<sup>9</sup></code></li>\n\t<li>The input is generated such that a majority element will exist in the array.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<strong>Follow-up:</strong> Could you solve the problem in linear time and in <code>O(1)</code> space?","h":[],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"majorityElement\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"nums\",\r\n      \"type\": \"integer[]\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"integer\"\r\n  }\r\n}","g":[{"name":"Array","slug":"array"},{"name":"Hash Table","slug":"hash-table"},{"name":"Divide and Conquer","slug":"divide-and-conquer"},{"name":"Sorting","slug":"sorting"},{"name":"Counting","slug":"counting"},{"name":"Boyer–Moore Majority Vote Algorithm","slug":"boyer-moore-majority-vote-algorithm"}],"s":[{"t":"Majority Element II","s":"majority-element-ii","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Check If a Number Is Majority Element in a Sorted Array","s":"check-if-a-number-is-majority-element-in-a-sorted-array","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Most Frequent Even Element","s":"most-frequent-even-element","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Minimum Index of a Valid Split","s":"minimum-index-of-a-valid-split","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Minimum Operations to Exceed Threshold Value I","s":"minimum-operations-to-exceed-threshold-value-i","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Find the Most Common Response","s":"find-the-most-common-response","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Find Valid Pair of Adjacent Digits in String","s":"find-valid-pair-of-adjacent-digits-in-string","d":"Easy","p":false}],"co":[["Amazon","amazon"],["Google","google"],["Bloomberg","bloomberg"],["Meta","facebook"],["Microsoft","microsoft"],["tcs","tcs"],["Accenture","accenture"],["Oracle","oracle"],["Qualcomm","qualcomm"],["Flipkart","flipkart"],["DE Shaw","de-shaw"],["Zoho","zoho"],["Autodesk","autodesk"],["Adobe","adobe"],["Zenefits","zenefits"]],"cs":{"a":[["Google","google",26],["Amazon","amazon",19],["Meta","facebook",7],["Microsoft","microsoft",6],["Bloomberg","bloomberg",6]],"b":[["Odoo","odoo",2]],"m":[["tcs","tcs",17],["Oracle","oracle",7],["Accenture","accenture",7],["Goldman Sachs","goldman-sachs",3],["Zoho","zoho",3],["DE Shaw","de-shaw",3],["Cognizant","cognizant",3],["Qualcomm","qualcomm",3],["IBM","ibm",2],["Adobe","adobe",2]]}}